    "ssky_text_block_TJmTzi": {
      "type": "ssky-text-block",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_b3byJW": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "<h2>Educational Books for 8th Graders That Prepare Kids for What’s Next</h2>",
            "custom_color": "",
            "alignment": "center",
            "heading_size": "h1",
            "heading_weight": "bold",
            "heading_tag": "h2",
            "center": false
          }
        },
        "text_XBeMcT": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "max_width": 100,
            "custom_color": "",
            "alignment": "left",
            "text": "<p>Our books for 8th graders help families as kids head toward high school with more independence, stronger judgment, and a growing desire to make sense of the world around them. At this stage, kids want stories that respect the fact that they’re noticing more, questioning more, and starting to connect ideas to the real world. We write stories that bring <a href=\"https://www.tuttletwins.com/collections/economics-for-kids\" title=\"https://www.tuttletwins.com/collections/economics-for-kids\">economics</a>, <a href=\"https://tuttletwins.com/collections/american-history-for-kids\" title=\"https://tuttletwins.com/collections/american-history-for-kids\">American history</a>, personal responsibility, and moral courage to life in ways that feel relatable and clear.</p><p>Our books for 8th graders are written for curious teens who are ready to ask bigger questions, think for themselves, and go beyond what a textbook alone can offer. And for parents, they create natural opportunities for thoughtful conversations around the dinner table about how the world works.</p>",
            "text_size": "medium",
            "text_weight": "regular"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_b3byJW",
        "text_XBeMcT"
      ],
      "name": "t:sections.ssky_text_block.name",
      "settings": {
        "content_alignment": "center",
        "max_width": 100,
        "color_scheme": "scheme-1",
        "twi_max_width": 120,
        "twi_margin": 20,
