        },
        "faq_9ehHzF": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<h5>Can I Use These Books in the Classroom or for Homeschool?</h5>",
            "text_size": "regular",
            "text_weight": "bold",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. Many parents and teachers use our books for group discussions, writing prompts, and history or civics enrichment. The stories open up meaningful discussions around economics, history, civics, and character in a way that feels approachable for middle schoolers and useful for the adults guiding them.</p>",
            "text_size_b": "medium",
            "text_weight_b": "regular"
          }
        },
        "faq_cELf8y": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<h5>How Do Tuttle Twins Books Help Prepare Kids for High School?</h5>",
            "text_size": "regular",
            "text_weight": "bold",
            "answer": "<p>Our books for 8th graders introduce bigger ideas in a way teens understand. Students practice thinking through choices, discussing viewpoints, and connecting ideas to real life. These skills help teens read more confidently, make thoughtful decisions, and step into high school with clearer judgment.</p>",
            "text_size_b": "medium",
            "text_weight_b": "regular"
          }
        },
        "faq_LM7xz8": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<h5>Looking for Something Else?</h5>",
            "text_size": "regular",
            "text_weight": "bold",
            "answer": "<p>No matter your child’s age, there’s a Tuttle Twins book that can help turn reading time into meaningful family conversations. Explore our economics and law books, or start with a combo pack that helps kids connect big ideas to real life in ways they can actually understand, and talk about with you.</p>",
            "text_size_b": "medium",
            "text_weight_b": "regular"
          }
        }
